Prerequisites
-------------

The following packages are needed:

  - A C++ compiler supporting C++26 (tested with GCC 16)
  - Boost (>= 1.70; only the header-only Boost.Asio is used)
  - gtkmm-4.0 (which itself needs GTK 4); available at https://www.gtkmm.org/
  - My YGP library (libYGP and libXGP, >= 0.9.50); also available as a
    Github project (https://github.com/pinche-gringo/libYGP)
  - Card decks; e.g. the KDE card games provide a huge collection. See also
    the README.

Optional:

  - librsvg 2 (to load SVG card decks, e.g. those of KDE)
  - Boost.Test (to build the unit tests and game simulations)


How to build
------------

Additional software needed to build:

  - Meson (>= 1.5) and Ninja
  - mgeni.pl (from the YGP library)
  - GNU gettext (for national language support)
  - ImageMagick (optional; to generate the application icons)

Inside the directory containing the source code, type

  meson setup build [meson-options]
  meson compile -C build
  meson install -C build


Common options for meson
------------------------

Options are passed to "meson setup" (or later to "meson configure build")
as -D<option>=<value>; "meson configure build" lists them all.

  --prefix=<path>               # Default: /usr/local
  -Dnls=disabled                # Disable national language support
  -Dnetwork=true                # Enable network capabilities
  -Dchecks=<level>              # Add asserts and internal checks
  -Ddebug-level=<level>         # Set the trace level & generate debug info
  -Dsaving=true                 # Games can be saved and loaded (for testing)
  -Drsvg=disabled               # Don't use librsvg to load SVG card decks
  -Dtests=disabled              # Don't build the unit tests and simulations
  -Dkde-carddir=<DIR>           # Path to the KDE card decks
  -Dgnome-carddir=<DIR>         # Path to the GNOME card decks
  -Dcardpics-dir=<DIR>          # Path to the "cardpics" card decks
  -D<game>=false                # Disable certain games (rovhult, twopart,
                                  hearts, buraco, machiavelli, sgtmayor,
                                  jabberwocky)

The card deck directories are detected automatically if not specified; pass
"no" to not use a certain kind of card deck.


Common commands
---------------

  meson install -C build        # Installs the whole thing
  meson test -C build           # Runs the unit tests (if built)
  ninja -C build clean          # Deletes the files created during the build
  ninja -C build uninstall      # Uninstalls (after you found out what crap
                                  this package actually contains)
  ninja -C build CardCol-update-po  # Updates the translations in po/
